  "limitations": "Convex shapes only; concave polygons must be split. No continuous (swept) collision: very fast objects can tunnel through thin walls in one step. Circle offsets and polygon offsets of SAT.js are not exposed. Results are for one moment; the game decides what a hit means.",
  "port_notes": "Port of SAT.js test functions with Vector math inlined. Response.clear() defaults (aInB=bInA=true, overlap=Number.MAX_VALUE) kept. Box is converted by Box.toPolygon. Polygon setPoints duplicate-point removal and setAngle rotation kept. Skillpack additions: input validation rejects clockwise, degenerate or concave polygons (SAT.js silently gives wrong answers there) and push_a = -overlapV.",
  "flow_role": "Step 11 (çarpışma kontrolü): check that spawn points do not sit inside buildings and define the push-out rule the game uses for car-vs-building tiles. The HTML runtime (G012) uses the same circle-vs-box formula; the end-to-end test compares them."
